        <groundspeak:log id="684684043">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP182 - Okotoks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for yet another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Lethbridge!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Along the way there and back. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Along the way to this cap a weird bright disk appeared in the sky.  Haven't seen such a thing in a while! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Then it was a short, enjoyable walk to find another disk. The geopooch found it first. Really. Then she tried to hide it from us. (I'll post proof pictures soon!)  Eventually we got what we needed and headed back to the car.  TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684659052">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP182 - Okotoks - Iron Phoenix and I discussed coming up from the bottom and decided we were both too tired to climb. We drove around to the top and took the longer, flatter way to the cap. On the way back Pippin was delighted to meet another Keeshond puppy in a nearby yard. The pup was 11 weeks old and cute as a button.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
